# Testing Requirements
Rule Type: Always

## Test Coverage Requirements
### Minimum Coverage
- Overall code coverage: 80%
- Critical paths: 90%
- Trading logic: 95%
- Error handling: 90%

### Critical Paths
- Signal generation
- Order execution
- Risk management
- Error handling
- Connection management

## Required Tests
### Unit Tests
- All strategy methods
- All IBKR connection methods
- All utility functions
- All data processing functions
- All error handling code

### Integration Tests
- IBKR connection
- Strategy execution
- Data flow
- Order management
- Error recovery

### Backtest Validation
- Historical data accuracy
- Signal generation
- Performance metrics
- Risk management
- Position sizing

## Test Categories
### Strategy Tests
- Indicator calculations
- Signal generation
- Entry/exit logic
- Risk management
- Position sizing

### Connection Tests
- Connection establishment
- Order placement
- Order cancellation
- Market data
- Error handling

### System Tests
- End-to-end workflows
- Performance under load
- Error recovery
- Data consistency
- System stability

## Test Requirements
### Test Data
- Use realistic market data
- Include edge cases
- Cover error conditions
- Include stress tests
- Maintain test datasets

### Test Environment
- Isolated test environment
- Paper trading mode
- Market data simulation
- Error injection capability
- Performance monitoring

### Test Documentation
- Test plan documentation
- Test case documentation
- Test results documentation
- Coverage reports
- Performance reports

## Validation Requirements
### Strategy Validation
- Compare with historical data
- Validate signal generation
- Verify risk management
- Check position sizing
- Monitor performance

### System Validation
- Verify data flow
- Check error handling
- Validate performance
- Monitor resource usage
- Test recovery procedures

## Performance Testing
### Latency Requirements
- Signal generation: < 100ms
- Order execution: < 500ms
- Data processing: < 50ms
- System response: < 200ms

### Resource Requirements
- Memory usage: < 1GB
- CPU usage: < 50%
- Network usage: < 1MB/s
- Disk usage: < 10GB

## Test Maintenance
### Regular Testing
- Run tests before deployment
- Schedule regular test runs
- Monitor test coverage
- Update test cases
- Review test results

### Test Updates
- Update tests with code changes
- Add new test cases
- Remove obsolete tests
- Maintain test data
- Update documentation
